  "body": "Implements MATHCERT #87 under MATH-PROGRAMME #237 from protected MATHSOLVE merge `3a8493aa322f0e640c921b8824c4d7f88a8c057d`.\n\n## Exact protected input\n\n- protected Solve reviewed head `cf2a46cb94419ed3ff9c0f078ee87e0e7ae0a9f8`;\n- candidate snapshot Git blob `af54ae9b9a047a36767b2599ebc649fb6fdaaa52`;\n- handoff Git blob `01a20512c428ce4384959064ab3343a1cbb0c7d2`;\n- campaign manifest Git blob `1cdb081595da2f8b21f60a192ec8cc83c20031ac`;\n- producer Git blob `012a90e0cd84e4ad7f0fd3f1c9534a6673dc0f24`.\n\n## Independent certification\n\nThe MATHCERT checker does not import or execute the Solve producer. It verifies exact upstream identities, input concordance, every Euclidean division equation, trace linkage, strict descent, terminal zero, positive normalization, divisibility, the integer B\u00e9zout equation, an independent `math.gcd` replay, and authority boundaries.\n\nFifteen focused tests retain malformed quotient, remainder, linkage, descent, truncation, divisor, coefficient, input, zero-case, identity, authority, protected-effect, and successor-activation failures.\n\n## Lean formalization\n\n`MathCert/Domains/NumberTheory/EuclidGCD.lean` defines the accepted-certificate predicate and proves:\n\n- accepted-certificate soundness: `d = Nat.gcd a b`;\n- the exact three-step trace;\n- `(-2 : Int) * 252 + 5 * 105 = 21`;\n- `Nat.gcd 252 105 = 21`;\n- the concrete accepted predicate and specialized soundness theorem.\n\nThe module contains no `sorry` and requests declaration-level axiom reports.\n\n## Route and documentary package\n\nThe proposed output is content-addressed at layer commit `9f55e7a5b9a4e082e18ccde927252ed79c11c11b`, Git blob `36c62434dbd19719d990e71ddc23729f0614ace7`. A successor route overlay preserves the protected base registry and VGSE overlay, registers only the Euclid claim family, and withholds protected effect until exact-head review, Human Steward disposition, and protected merge.\n\nThe Chaidez-oriented note preserves object, construction, witness, and certificate separation; exact historical Book VII attribution remains deferred to the mandatory source-lock stage.\n\n## Boundaries\n\nThis PR does not prove total correctness of every extended-Euclidean implementation, attribute the modern integer B\u00e9zout identity verbatim to Euclid, claim novelty or priority, or activate the linear Diophantine or Book VII successor stages.\n\nTarget disposition after exact-head CI, independent approval, and Human Steward authorization:\n\n`CERTIFIED_CHECKER_SOUNDNESS_AND_CONCRETE_GCD_INSTANCE`",
